    "q-26917": {
      "dom_id": "step-q26917",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer. \n\nI. The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\nII. The function has minimum values at $x=…-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2},\\frac{7\\pi }{2}...$\n\nIII. The range of the function is $y\\in [-1,1].$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255188/assets/776d667a77d544cb8fef10ad1c0b3fc625afa75e97f3203d41aefea5ff0c08d0.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The minimum values of the function occur at $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is true. The minimum value is $-1,$ the maximum value is $1,$ and so the range is $y\\in [-1,1].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
