    "q-103201": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103201",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "If $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3},$ then $6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-12\\pi )=$",
      "worked_solution": "The period of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-6$ into the left-hand-side gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-12\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3},$ then $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-12\\pi )=-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}.$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-12\\pi )=6(-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3})=-2\\sqrt{6}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-103201-a",
